# GMS names the same five conditions Storm Magic does, and pays 5+x% against
# an enemy under any of them. The F/P has the other of the two this game keeps:
# a burn. So it collects on whatever Poison Breath, Poison Mist, Flame Sweep or
# Ifrit has left alight -- which is nearly everything the class fights, and is
# meant to be.
#
# GMS's other half is dropped: it lengthens every burn by 50+5x%, and a burn
# already outlasts the swing that relights it, so nothing here would change.
name: "Burning Magic"
skill_order: 7
description:
  "Increases your Final Damage against enemies taking continuous damage."
kind: SKILL_KIND_PASSIVE
job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_FIRE_POISON_MAGE
max_level: 10
base { final_dmg_pct_when_afflicted: 0.06 }
per_level { final_dmg_pct_when_afflicted: 0.01 }
